"""Preparation oracle for FlagGems ``special_bessel_j0`` (reference-as-solution).

ABI served by this file (single positional Tensor in, Tensor out):

* accuracy  -- ``tests/test_special_bessel_j0.py`` calls
  ``flag_gems.special_bessel_j0(inp)``; the formal override
  ``--override special_bessel_j0:<this file>:run`` rebinds that public export to
  ``run`` through ``flag_gems.dynamic_registry.DynamicOpOverride``.
* benchmark -- ``benchmark/base.py::Benchmark._candidate_call()`` resolves the
  same override by ``op_name`` (``special_bessel_j0``), so the timed candidate is
  ``run`` as well.

This module deliberately imports only ``torch``: the preparation oracle must not
import ``flag_gems`` and therefore can never re-enter the operator it replaces.

Oracle semantics: ``torch.special.bessel_j0`` is exactly the expression the
frozen accuracy test already uses as its reference
(``ref_out = torch.special.bessel_j0(ref_inp)``). It returns a new Tensor that
keeps the input dtype/device/shape and neither mutates nor aliases the input,
matching the frozen Definition (``mutates: []``, ``returns_alias_of: {}``).
"""

import torch


def run(x):
    """Elementwise Bessel function of the first kind of order zero."""
    return torch.special.bessel_j0(x)
